\par\pard\plain \tx0\tx360\tx720\tx1080\tx1440\tx1800\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\li763\fi-475\sa240\ql\ltrch\loch {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 <$Scr_Ps::0>\bullet \tab The list on the left is called the }{\f3\fs22\b1\i0\cf4 <$Scr_Cs::1>binder<!$Scr_Cs::1>}{\f1\fs24\b0\i0 , because it acts as the project\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92s ring-binder, being where you file and organise all of your material.}
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 \bullet \tab The }{\f3\fs22\b1\i0\cf4 <$Scr_Cs::1>editor<!$Scr_Cs::1>}{\f1\fs24\b0\i0  contains the text you are reading right now, and is where you\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92ll do all your writing. It can also show research documents, such as images and PDF files.}
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 \bullet \tab If you click on the \loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8220\'93i\u8221\'94 in the right of the toolbar (the strip of buttons at the top of the window), you\u8217\'92ll open the }{\f3\fs22\b1\i0\cf4 <$Scr_Cs::1>inspector<!$Scr_Cs::1>}{\f1\fs24\b0\i0 . The inspector displays information relating to the document currently shown in the editor, such as its synopsis, label and status.<!$Scr_Ps::0>}
\par\pard\plain \tx0\tx360\tx720\tx1080\tx1440\tx1800\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\sa360\sl264\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 Let\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92s start by looking at the binder in a little more detail\hich\f1 \emdash \loch\f1 in the binder sidebar, click on the document entitled \u8220\'93The Binder\u8221\'94.}}